 JobParametersValidator
A job declared in the XML namespace or using any subclass of AbstractJob can optionally declare a validator for the job parameters at runtime. 
This is useful when for instance you need to assert that a job is started with all its mandatory parameters. 
There is a DefaultJobParametersValidator that can be used to constrain combinations of simple mandatory and optional parameters, 
and for more complex constraints you can implement the interface yourself. 
The configuration of a validator is supported through the XML namespace through a child element of the job, 
e.g:
@Bean(name = "firstBatchJob")
	public Job firstBatchJob(@Qualifier("step1")Step step1,
			@Qualifier("step2")Step step2, 
			@Qualifier("step3_error")Step step3,
			@Qualifier("step4")Step step4,
			@Qualifier("msd_decider")MSDDecider msdDecider,
			MSDJobParameterValidator jobParameterValidator) {
		return jobBuilderFactory.get("firstBatchJob")
					.validator(jobParameterValidator)
					.start(step1)
					.next(step2)
					.next(msdDecider)
					.from(msdDecider).on("FAILED").to(step3)
					.from(msdDecider).on("COMPLETED").to(step4)
					.end()
					.build();
	}
The validator can be specified as a reference (as above) or as a nested bean/Inner bean definition in the beans namespace.

